/-!
# R-52CF5DA1 stage 13b: the local propagation estimate at a rough center

`prop:audit-finite-count-propagation` (GAUGE_RETARGETING.tex:101), assembled at one unit rough center `u_*` from the
proof paragraphs "All these quantum operators commute ... compares the true count evolution with
`exp(-iNΣ t_nC^{(0)}_{N,n})` with uniform vector error" (stage 13a), "A4's functional-linearization lemma ... compare
the fixed marginals with those generated by the bounded interaction series `N Σ t_n L^v_{N,n}` ... up to scalar terms"
(stage 12), "Its interaction kernels have one common factorial majorant because the contours are fixed and `|D_v|` has
a common positive lower bound. A2's bounded-interaction propagation theorem therefore applies uniformly there"
(stage 5 and the accepted PROP-001 schedule rate), and "The limiting Hamiltonian is the corresponding linear
functional of the classical transfer with denominator frozen at `v` ... identifies this flow with `T_t`" (stage 8b).

* `evol_near_r`: stage 13a with a label-dependent tube radius (the accepted PROP-010 existence theorem gives one
  radius per label; proof verbatim);
* `norm_countEvol`, `norm_frozenEvol`: both evolutions are unitary (diagonal with real eigenvalues);
* `traceNorm_three`: the three-term trace-norm triangle inequality;
* **`local_rate`**: for a unit rough center `u`, a finite label set `F`, a time box `|t_n| ≤ T_n` and a rank `k`,
  there are a neighborhood `U ∋ u`, a rate `ρ_N → 0` and `N₀` such that for all `N ≥ N₀`, unit `v ∈ U` and all real
  `t` vanishing off `F` in the box, `‖γ^{(k)}_{exp(-iΣ t_n M_{N,n}) v^{⊗N}} - |(T_t v)^{⊗k}⟩⟨(T_t v)^{⊗k}|‖₁ ≤ ρ_N`.
  The extensions are those of the accepted PROP-010 existence theorem (rectangle height 1); the chart statement
  `GlobalStatement` is a hypothesis here and is supplied from the accepted R-F5355ABD theorem in stage 14.
No other hypothesis is added; all inherited modules are read-only.
-/

